        "original_id": "b34cb331-493a-5434-b035-2b8ab0164e10",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: EdChoice, Cato Institute Center for Educational Freedom\n- People: Milton Friedman, Rose Director Friedman, Jason Bedrick, Anna J. Schwartz\n- Roles: Director of Policy, adjunct scholar, policy analyst, economist\n- Products: A Monetary History of the United States, 1867–1960\n- Topics: Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences\n\nFacts:\n- Milton Friedman and Anna J. Schwartz wrote A Monetary History of the United States, 1867–1960 in 1963.\n- Milton Friedman received the 1976 Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for research on consumption analysis, monetary history and theory, and the complexity of stabilization policy.\n- EdChoice was founded in 1996 by Milton Friedman and Rose Director Friedman.\n- Jason Bedrick is the Director of Policy at EdChoice.\n- Jason Bedrick is an adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom.\n- Jason Bedrick was previously a policy analyst at the Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom.",
